# Whether a double is an int32 is one comparison: the low half of the truncated number, made a double again, has the bits of the number. A number outside of int32, a fraction, NaN, an infinity and -0 all differ from it, so the range needs no test of its own (3 instructions less)
# FORM: Selected
# OPTIONS: check=validate-back-end
# RUN: generate-code
# CHECK: f0: size=
# RUN(X64): generate-code
# REQUIRES(X64): x86_64
# X64: f0: size=35 frame=none

module m0 path="main.js" displayPath="main.js"
function f0 name="isInt32" parameters=[{type=number}] results=[{type=int}] {
    v1 = TypeTest v0 testedType=i32
    Branch v1 -> taken b1(), notTaken b2()
  b1():
    v2 = Integer integer=1
    Return v2
  b2():
    v3 = Integer integer=0
    Return v3
}
